Image-default system credentials.

systemd resolves a unit's ImportCredential=/LoadCredential= against, first
match winning (exec-credential.c, credential_search_path):

    /run/credentials/@system/   system credentials (SMBIOS, qemu, initrd)
    /etc/credstore/             operator, on the /etc overlay upper
    /run/credstore/
    /usr/lib/credstore/         this directory — the image default

So a value here is a DEFAULT. Note it beats an ESP credential of the same
name — measured — so a name defaulted here is NOT overridable before first
boot. That is the right trade only for values every host can start with and
change later at runtime:

  passwd.hashed-password.root   `changeme`, so an unstaged host still has a
                                console login. Change it with `passwd`.
  firstboot.timezone            written to /etc/localtime on first boot.
                                Change it with `timedatectl set-timezone`.

Both land on the /etc overlay upper and survive image upgrades, and
systemd-firstboot never runs again (ConditionFirstBoot=yes), so neither
default can come back and clobber the host's choice.

Anything that must differ per host BEFORE first boot must have no default
here — see credentials/ in the repo.

WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY
-------------------------
A default belongs here only when its consumer can actually reach it. On
systemd 259 most cannot, verified by booting a VM:

  hostname   no firstboot.hostname or system.hostname credential exists in
             259 at all (they are newer). /etc/hostname is baked instead
             and overridden per host by a tmpfiles.extra credential.
  locale     /etc/locale.conf ships in an RPM, so it is in the image no
             matter what mkosi.extra does, and firstboot skips a value
             that is already set. Baked via mkosi.conf Locale=.
  keymap     same, /etc/vconsole.conf. It also overrides the vconsole.*
             credentials outright (vconsole-setup reads the file last).

The rule the hard way: deleting a file from mkosi.extra/etc/ does NOT
remove it from the image. mkosi.finalize snapshots the build-settled /etc,
RPM-provided files included.

Filenames here carry NO .cred suffix — that exists only on the ESP.
